This repository is the BlueClip statute dataset: a curated, categorized, and
structured compilation of Canadian legislation prepared for the BlueClip
application (the "Dataset").

1. Source law
   The underlying statutes, regulations, and bylaws are Crown or municipal works,
   reproduced under their respective licences — including the King's Printer
   Licence (British Columbia), the Reproduction of Federal Law Order (SI/97-5),
   and applicable municipal bylaw permissions. Those licences and their terms
   continue to govern the underlying legal text, and nothing here claims
   ownership of the underlying law itself.

2. BlueClip's contribution
   The selection, arrangement, categorization, plain-language summaries,
   cross-references, tagging, and overall data structure in these files are
   original works of authorship and a compilation, protected by copyright and
   owned by BlueClip. This contribution is the "Dataset" for the purposes of
   these terms.

3. No redistribution or reuse
   Except as the source-law licences in Section 1 permit for the underlying
   legal text, you may not copy, redistribute, republish, scrape, mirror, host,
   sell, sublicense, or create derivative works from the Dataset, in whole or in
   part, for any purpose (commercial or non-commercial), without BlueClip's prior
   written permission. Access to this repository is provided solely to serve the
   BlueClip application.

4. No warranty
   The Dataset is provided "AS IS", for reference only. It is not legal advice
   and may contain errors or omissions. Always verify against the official source
   before relying on it. To the maximum extent permitted by law, BlueClip
   disclaims all warranties and is not liable for any loss arising from its use.

